course: dictionary
lesson: 1329
title: Calm and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one. Calm can describe a person, the weather, the sea, or a quiet time. «Stay calm and think before you act.» Here calm means not worried, angry or excited.
explain: «The sea was calm, with no waves at all.» The sea is not a person, so calm means still, without wind or waves. Ask yourself what the word describes: a person, a place, or a time?
explain: Calm can also be a verb, a doing word. «Breathing slowly helps you calm down when you are scared.» Here calm down means to become peaceful again. The small word down changes how calm is used.
explain: Some people say «don't have a cow» to mean calm down. You cannot guess that from the single words, but the context shows it is about feeling upset. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Calm means not worried, angry or excited; it also means peaceful.
fact: In weather, calm means there is no wind.
fact: As a noun, calm means a peaceful, quiet time, as in «the calm before the storm».
fact: As a verb, to calm someone or something means to make them peaceful, as in «calm down».
fact: Calm can change form: calmer and calmest compare how peaceful something is.
exercise: «The sea was calm this morning.» What does calm mean here? | Angry and loud | *Still, without wind or waves | Excited about the day | Worried about the boat
exercise: «Stay calm, think, and follow the plan.» What does calm mean here? | *Not worried, angry or excited | Loud and noisy | Lost in a crowd | Very cold
exercise: Maya says, «Breathing slowly helps you calm down.» Which word is the verb in calm down? | slowly | you | breathing | *calm
test: «There was a calm before the storm.» Here calm is a noun. What does it mean? | A strong wind | *A peaceful, quiet time | A loud shout | A dark cloud
test: «The lake is calmer today than yesterday.» What does calmer mean? | More lost | More angry | More excited | *More peaceful, with less wind or waves
exam: Lily says, «Don't have a cow», when Maddie is upset. What does she mean? | *Calm down | Get a pet cow | Ask for a cow | Run away from home
